# USB Subsystem Status (0401826)

Date: 2026-04-19
Basis: Live source code audit only (no reliance on docs/historic)

## Executive Summary

The current USB implementation is a strong host-controller discovery and root-port bring-up scaffold, but it is not yet a full USB stack. The system can discover USB host controllers, perform guarded reset/halt/start sequences, scan/service root ports, synthesize candidate device rows, and expose broad observability via /proc. It now includes descriptor-accurate interface-aware class routing with rebind reconciliation plus a first bind-scoped bulk queue/retry state machine for RTL815x, cached xHCI bulk transport state, timer-driven runtime servicing from the kernel tick path, and split bulk submit/reap plumbing, but still lacks production transfer scheduling and class-driver datapaths.

Estimated overall maturity: 83%

